{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMiFdkeQmhzXic7ZFkFo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed both review findings and the owner's must-fix (the scanner failing on every real run), and wrote the report to `.ard/224/worker-engineer.md`.\n\n**Tests**\n- The package tests for roles, executor, executor/local, config, scanner and initcmd pass.\n- The new Docker test and the real-trufflehog test (3.100.0) pass here.\n- I ran `gofmt -l` but not `make lint`, so lint on the changed files is unchecked.\n\n**Review findings**\n- **Docker integration test:** `TestDockerHistory` in `internal/executor/local/docker_integration_test.go` now runs `git --git-dir /history log --all` in a container. It checks that it sees more than one commit and that a write to `/history` fails. That the read-only mount works for git in a container is now tested, and the `safe.directory` setting works.\n- **Host-mode comment:** the comments on `Job.History`, `Paths.History` and `Prepare` now say host mode does not enforce read-only.\n\n**Owner's security review**\n- **Missing `--bare`:** `scan` now passes `--bare` to `trufflehog git`. I updated `TestTrufflehogHistoryArgv` and `docs/proposal.md` to match.\n- **Real-binary test:** `TestTrufflehogHistoryRealBinary` runs real trufflehog against a bare repo whose refs live only under `refs/ard/*`. It expects one finding, no secret on stdout or stderr, and a clean TMPDIR. It skips when trufflehog isn't installed, and the credential-shaped values are built at run time.\n- **Issue text:** it now says the value may be only on an unmerged branch ard fetched, so it may not have reached main.\n\n**Not done**\n- I did not add a separate killed-mid-stream test for the history scanner. The existing fail-closed cases (non-zero exit, missing summary line) cover truncated output.\n- The choice of a read-only mount over a `git bundle` is still for a maintainer to confirm."}],"container":null,